# Overview
#
# An intensifier is the grammar term for an adverb that strengthens a
# claim (`very`, `really`). An adverb is a word that describes a verb,
# an adjective, or a whole sentence, such as `safely` or `also`. An
# intensifier raises a claim without measuring it, so the reader cannot
# tell how much the word adds. The fix drops the word (`a very large
# file` becomes `a large file`), or gives a number that stays true, such
# as a limit that a protocol sets. The rule sits at Optional, because
# each word here sometimes carries meaning.
#
# Expression
#
# `very` skips a preceding `the`, `this`, or `that`. Weir has no
# lookbehind, so the filter consumes the word before `very` and narrows
# the finding back to `very`.
#
# False Positives
#
# After `the`, `this`, or `that`, `very` means exact (`the very first
# entry`), so it passes. The adjective `genuine` stays out, because it
# usually means authentic (`the badge in the footer is genuine`).
#
# `genuinely` sometimes separates a real case from an apparent one (`a
# line is added only when the file genuinely ends in a blank line`), so
# it sits at Optional.
#
# Related Rules
#
# The Optional ProseIntensifier holds the intensifiers that sometimes
# carry meaning, such as `actually`. The Recommended ProseIntensifier
# holds every other intensifier.
#
# `very`, `really`, `truly`, and `actually` sit at Optional too, because
# each hit 14 to 139 lines in the measure.py corpus, and `actually`
# often marks a real contrast.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 318 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 15 of 20 sampled
# hits read as well without the word. The other 5 used `actually` for a
# real contrast with what the reader expects (`the number of bytes
# actually written`), as in `the file is actually a symlink`.
expr main [genuinely, <(![the, this, that] very), very>, really, truly, actually]
let message "Intensifier. Delete the word, or give a number that stays true, such as a protocol limit."
let description "Flags `genuinely`, `very`, `really`, `truly`, and `actually`, which usually raise a claim without informing."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The badge in the footer is genuine."
allows "The path is contended under load."
allows "The very first entry holds the header."
